 ░▒▓█ what is it ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

   strike, bow or lean on a virtual plate: bronze, steel, glass, wood, 24
   objects in all. dozens of real vibration modes ring out, and the sand
   on the screen settles on the nodal lines of exactly what you hear. one
   physics engine draws the picture and makes the sound. no samples, no
   fake animation.

 ░▒▓█ features ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

   + modal synthesis, band-limited by nature    + sand / field / mesh views
   + melt the plate: circle > hex > star live   + cymatic + phosphor themes
   + pressure, bow and damp, played by hand     + team eg bronze bell at boot
   + usb sounds tool, backups, sharing codes    + plays in your browser too

 ░▒▓█ install ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

   read notes/INSTALL.md first. back up the whole flash. check the sha-256.
   never install m-vave's v16 on a unit you want to run this on.
   try it first, no synth needed:  teg-lizard-man.github.io/cyma-1

